What happens if two engineers run terraform apply at the same time?

If terrafor.tfstate is stored in remote AWS S3 bucket and lock is enabled then below is the process terraform does:

Engineer 1:
-----------------
- When Engineer1 runs terraform apply then state lock acquired
- Engineer 2 will wait until lock is released
- Changes will be made in cloud (AWS, Azure GCP etc.,)
- Update State
- Release Lock

Engineer 2:
--------------------
- lock aquired
- Changes will be made in cloud
- Update state
- Release lock
- When Engineer2 acquired lock other engineers will be in waiting state

This process repeats for any number of tasks.

If lock is not released for any cases, Your process should be:

1. Check failed GitHub Actions job
2. Confirm Terraform process is no longer running
3. Check lock ID / timestamp
4. Confirm no other apply is running
5. Force-unlock
6. Run terraform plan
7. Review carefully
8. Apply through CI/CD

Note: Never force-unlock until I prove that no Terraform operation is using that state.
